  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Land administration 2013-2019, Mozambique,        GESTERRA - GESTERRA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Markadministration 2013-2019, Mo&#xE7;ambique,      GESTERRA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">GESTERRA var ett program som implementerades mellan 2013 och 2019, med syfte att etablera v&#xE4;l utformat, reglerat, transparent och implementerat markf&#xF6;rvaltningssystem baserad p&#xE5; inkluderande ekonomisk och social utveckling. Programmet hade tv&#xE5; huvudkomponenter: (i) markf&#xF6;rvaltning som fr&#xE4;mjar en integrerad vision av markadministration och styrning, och (ii) markf&#xF6;rvaltningstj&#xE4;nster och skapandet av landstadsregistret.

Programmet fokuserade p&#xE5; institutionell kapacitetsuppbyggnad, systemutveckling och decentraliserad utrullning av markf&#xF6;rvaltningssystemet. Genom DINAT, det nationella fastighetsregistret i Mo&#xE7;ambique (&apos;Direc&#xE7;&#xE3;o Nacional de Terras), skulle Mo&#xE7;ambiques regering kunna leda markf&#xF6;rvaltningsprocessen och spela en kritisk och konstruktiv roll i markf&#xF6;rvaltningen, med f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrad kommunikation och uppr&#xE4;tth&#xE5;llande av tekniska normer och standarder f&#xF6;r markf&#xF6;rvaltning, samt &#xF6;vervakning och kvalitetskontroll.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GESTERRA was a programme that was implemented between 2013 and 2019, aiming to establish a well-designed and regulated, transparent and implemented land governance system as the basis for inclusive social and economic development. The programme had two main components: (i) Land governance for an integrated vision of land management and land administration, and (ii) Land administration services and building of the National Land Cadastre.

The programme focused on institutional capacity building, system development, and de-centralised roll-out of the land administration system. Through DINAT, the National Land Registry in Mozambique (the &apos;Direc&#xE7;&#xE3;o Nacional de Terras), the Government of Mozambique would be able to lead the land management process and play a critical and constructive role in land governance, with improved communication and enforcement of technical norms and standards for land administration, as well as monitoring and quality control.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GESTERRA was a programme that was implemented between 2013 and 2019, aiming to establish a well-designed and regulated, transparent and implemented land governance system as the basis for inclusive social and economic development. The programme had two main components: (i) Land governance for an integrated vision of land management and land administration, and (ii) Land administration services and building of the National Land Cadastre.

The programme focused on institutional capacity building, system development, and de-centralised roll-out of the land administration system. Through DINAT, the National Land Registry in Mozambique (the &apos;Direc&#xE7;&#xE3;o Nacional de Terras), the Government of Mozambique would be able to lead the land management process and play a critical and constructive role in land governance, with improved communication and enforcement of technical norms and standards for land administration, as well as monitoring and quality control.</narrative>
  </description>
